WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.980
At ocean-ocean convergence, one plate descends, commonly the older, colder, denser

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.190
one. Use density and temperature to explain which plate sinks.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:15.597
At ocean-continent convergence, dense oceanic lithosphere subducts beneath more buoyant continental

00:00:15.597 --> 00:00:19.890
crust. Identify the plate types before naming the process.

00:00:20.725 --> 00:00:25.697
Two continents resist deep subduction. Collision shortens and thickens their crust,

00:00:25.697 --> 00:00:30.669
building mountains. Remember India, Asia, and the Himalaya as the review

00:00:30.669 --> 00:00:31.121
example.
